# ConfigStore Usage
RULE: Use ConfigStore for runtime config (service params). Import from unified_trading_services (moved from unified_config_interface in v1.1.0).
WHY: Enables persistence and hot reload for service parameters. UCI is now Level 0 (no cloud deps); UCS owns cloud persistence.
CODEX: 06-coding-standards/config-types.md, 05-infrastructure/unified-libraries/LIBRARY-DEPENDENCY-MATRIX.md
DO:
  from unified_trading_services import ConfigStore, ConfigReloader, TimeSeriesConfigStore
  store = ConfigStore(bucket_name, service_name, schema_version)
  reloader = ConfigReloader(MyServiceConfig, service_name, callback, project_id=config.gcp_project_id)
NEVER:
  from unified_config_interface import ConfigStore  # MOVED to unified_trading_services
  from unified_config_interface import ConfigReloader  # MOVED to unified_trading_services
  Use grid config for runtime params; skip ConfigStore for services with hot-reloadable config
